<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husayn Ali Khan of Quba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1758</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Husayn Ali Khan was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quba">Quba</a> in the north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> in 1747 he ruled as an effectively independent khan and moved his seat to the new town of Quba. His son Fatali Khan, who succeeded him in 1758, made the Quba Khanate the strongest power in the region.</p></div>
